  <p>That disagreement is not academic. If the lower parts are water, the work is to push them back and hold the line, forever, against a sea that is always rising. If they are strings, the work is to tune them, and a tuned string is not a defeated one. Odysseus, lying in the dark, did not drain his heart. He spoke to it, and it held, and in the morning it was the same heart that strung the bow.</p>
</section>

<section class="mv" id="m6" data-t="The man inside the man">
  <div class="wm" aria-hidden="true">VI</div>
  <h2><span>VI.</span> The man inside the man</h2>
  <p>There is a third witness between Athens and Vienna, and he writes in the same Greek.</p>
  <p><span class="tag text" data-tip="Rep. IX 588b–589b">text</span> Plato closes the argument of the <em>Republic</em> with a picture (588b–589b): imagine a creature that is a many-headed beast, a lion, and a man, all sewn inside the skin of a man, so that from outside you see only the man. The beast is appetite, the lion is thumos, and the little man within is reason. The unjust man feeds the beast and starves the man; the just man makes <span lang="grc">ὁ ἐντὸς ἄνθρωπος</span>, “the man inside,” the master of the whole animal (589a).</p>

  <div class="play figure" data-label="Rep. 588b–589b · the creature">
    <div class="figwrap">
      <svg class="figsvg" viewBox="0 0 300 460" role="img" aria-label="A human outline drawn as a constellation. Inside it, low in the body, a many-headed beast; above it a lion; in the chest a small man, faintly pulsing.">
        <defs>
          <pattern id="wiwDither" width="5" height="5" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><circle cx="2.5" cy="2.5" r=".65" fill="#e6dfcf" fill-opacity=".13"/></pattern>
          <clipPath id="wiwBody"><circle cx="150" cy="55" r="30"/><path d="M118 90C100 100 80 110 72 150L60 250l20 5 12-85v130l8 140h35l15-120 15 120h35l8-140V170l12 85 20-5-12-100c-8-40-28-50-46-60z"/></clipPath>
        </defs>
        <g clip-path="url(#wiwBody)"><rect width="300" height="460" fill="url(#wiwDither)"/></g>
        <g class="outline"><circle cx="150" cy="55" r="30"/><path d="M118 90C100 100 80 110 72 150L60 250l20 5 12-85v130l8 140h35l15-120 15 120h35l8-140V170l12 85 20-5-12-100c-8-40-28-50-46-60"/></g>
        <g class="beast">
          <g class="hair"><path d="M150 330l-30 15m30-15l30 15m-30-15l-15 45m15-45l15 45m-45-30l15 30m45-30l-15 30M150 330l-45-30m45 30l-30-45m30 45l-12-52m12 52v-55m0 55l12-52m-12 52l30-45m-30 45l45-30"/></g>
          <g class="star"><circle cx="150" cy="330" r="3"/><circle cx="120" cy="345" r="2.4"/><circle cx="180" cy="345" r="2.4"/><circle cx="135" cy="375" r="2.4"/><circle cx="165" cy="375" r="2.4"/></g>
          <g class="head"><circle cx="105" cy="300" r="3.2"/><circle cx="120" cy="285" r="3.2"/><circle cx="138" cy="278" r="3.2"/><circle cx="150" cy="275" r="3.2"/><circle cx="162" cy="278" r="3.2"/><circle cx="180" cy="285" r="3.2"/><circle cx="195" cy="300" r="3.2"/></g>
        </g>
        <g class="lion">
          <g class="hair"><path d="M150 172l16.5 5.4 10.2 14-0 17.3-10.2 14-16.5 5.4-16.5-5.4-10.2-14 0-17.3 10.2-14zM150 172v-10m16.5 5.4l6-8m10.2 14l9-4m0 17.3l10 1m-10.2 14l7 7m-16.5 5.4l3 9m-16.5-5.4v10m-16.5-5.4l-3 9m-10.2-14l-7 7m0-17.3l-10 1m0-17.3l-9-4m10.2-14l-6-8"/><path d="M142 196l8 12 8-12"/></g>
          <g class="star"><circle cx="150" cy="172" r="2.2"/><circle cx="166.5" cy="177.4" r="2.2"/><circle cx="176.7" cy="191.4" r="2.2"/><circle cx="176.7" cy="208.7" r="2.2"/><circle cx="166.5" cy="222.7" r="2.2"/><circle cx="150" cy="228.1" r="2.2"/><circle cx="133.5" cy="222.7" r="2.2"/><circle cx="123.3" cy="208.7" r="2.2"/><circle cx="123.3" cy="191.4" r="2.2"/><circle cx="133.5" cy="177.4" r="2.2"/><circle cx="142" cy="196" r="2.6"/><circle cx="158" cy="196" r="2.6"/><circle cx="150" cy="208" r="2"/></g>
